From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:02:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] agent: service WSC M2 recovery after orchestration

The bounded M1 retry added for a lost WSC M2 is reached through
handle_agent_state(), which first requires an active orchestration command.
That lifetime is not a reliable proxy for the radio protocol state: one radio
can complete the shared device-init operation while sibling radios remain in
wsc_m2_pending. Those radios continue receiving protocol ticks, but the
orchestration guard discards every tick and no M1 is retried.

Service wsc_m2_pending directly from the per-radio protocol timeout. The radio
state remains the ownership boundary, so reception of M2 changes state and
stops retries immediately. All other Agent states keep the existing
orchestration-command guard.

The M1 encoder also used the active command to obtain its local AL MAC and
device-identity attributes. Use the radio's persistent data-model accessors
instead, since a recovery transaction intentionally outlives that command.
The values are identical during ordinary onboarding and remain valid
afterward.

This recovered a reproducible tri-band extender that otherwise remained at
three radios, nine BSS records and only two operational fronthaul BSSs after
one of its three initial M2 frames was lost.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hwsim lab protocol recovery]
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 14 +++++++-------
 src/em/em.cpp                       | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/em/em.cpp b/src/em/em.cpp
index 52e6d7a..64130ad 100644
--- a/src/em/em.cpp
+++ b/src/em/em.cpp
@@ -608,6 +608,16 @@ void em_t::proto_timeout()
 {
     if (m_service_type == em_service_type_agent) {
+        // WSC is a per-radio protocol transaction. A sibling radio can
+        // complete the shared device-init orchestration while this radio is
+        // still waiting for M2, so the orchestration lifetime must not gate
+        // its bounded M1 recovery timer. The state transition performed on
+        // M2 reception remains the self-clearing stop condition.
+        if (m_sm.get_state() == em_state_agent_wsc_m2_pending) {
+            em_configuration_t::process_agent_state();
+            return;
+        }
+
         handle_agent_state();
     } else if (m_service_type == em_service_type_ctrl) {
         handle_ctrl_state();
     }
diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
index 42d97f4..99af3fd 100644
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -3653 +3653 @@ unsigned short em_configuration_t::create_m1_msg(unsigned char *buff)
-	str = get_current_cmd()->get_manufacturer();
+	str = get_manufacturer();
@@ -3664 +3664 @@ unsigned short em_configuration_t::create_m1_msg(unsigned char *buff)
-	str = get_current_cmd()->get_manufacturer_model();
+	str = get_manufacturer_model();
@@ -3675 +3675 @@ unsigned short em_configuration_t::create_m1_msg(unsigned char *buff)
-	str = get_current_cmd()->get_manufacturer_model();
+	str = get_manufacturer_model();
@@ -3686 +3686 @@ unsigned short em_configuration_t::create_m1_msg(unsigned char *buff)
-	str = get_current_cmd()->get_serial_number();
+	str = get_serial_number();
@@ -3699 +3699 @@ unsigned short em_configuration_t::create_m1_msg(unsigned char *buff)
-    memcpy(attr->val, get_current_cmd()->get_primary_device_type(), size);
+    memcpy(attr->val, get_primary_device_type(), size);
@@ -3707 +3707 @@ unsigned short em_configuration_t::create_m1_msg(unsigned char *buff)
-	str = get_current_cmd()->get_manufacturer_model();
+	str = get_manufacturer_model();
@@ -4431 +4431 @@ int em_configuration_t::create_autoconfig_wsc_m1_msg(unsigned char *buff, unsign
-    memcpy(tmp, get_current_cmd()->get_al_interface_mac(), sizeof(mac_address_t));
+    memcpy(tmp, get_al_interface_mac(), sizeof(mac_address_t));
